Store a small destructor identifier in each handle list instead of the
destructor's address.  Lists live in handle memory, which mh_Dump writes to
the save file and mh_ReLoad restores verbatim, so a saved address belonged
to the process that wrote it.  A position-independent executable loads at a
different base each run: the restored game then jumped through the stale
address as soon as a list freed an element (SIGSEGV in DestroySpells at
exit, and equally when an actor with timers died).

mhdlist_destroy looks the identifier up in a fixed table and range-checks
it, since the value comes from a file.  The list header changes size, so the
save magic changes too and saves in the original layout take the existing
corrupt-save path instead of being misread.  Nix channel maintenance patch,
applied after the gcc16-io patch.

